```

Answer: We should use an if-else statement when: There are two possible statements or blocks. One block must be executed when the condition is true. The other block must be executed when the condition is false. Exactly one block should execute at a given point in time. Example:

```java
if (age >= 18) {
System.out.println("You are eligible for voting");
