Answer: An else-if ladder is a conditional control construct used when there are multiple conditions and multiple possible blocks of statements. The conditions are checked one by one. When a condition becomes true, its block is executed, and the remaining conditions are skipped. Syntax:

```java
if (condition1) {
// statements
```

} else if (condition2) {

```java
// statements
```

} else if (condition3) {

```java
// statements
```

} else {

```java
// default statements
}
```

Answer: The final else block is used to handle all values that do not satisfy any of the previous conditions. It acts as the default block. Example:

